# English translations of the "Informatie & Tips" articles (source: the Dutch articles on pc-spain.com).
A_ = lambda s: f'en-article-{s}.html'
EN_ARTICLES = {
 'aankoopmakelaar-spanje': ('Buyer’s agent in Spain', f'''<p><a href="{A_('huis-kopen-in-spanje')}">Buying a house in Spain</a>. It sounds like a dream, but we make it reality. With our team of independent consultants and experienced agents we support you through the <a href="{A_('procedure-aankoop-woning-spanje')}">buying process</a>. We offer expertise in several fields, so we do more than just the purchase: besides purchase guidance we also provide legal advice. That guarantees you a transparent process with clear agreements. This is how we make buying a house in Spain accessible to you – after all, the purchase procedure there is very different from the Netherlands.</p><h2>Hiring a buyer’s agent in Spain</h2><p>Buying a house involves all kinds of things, which leaves plenty of room for mistakes – not what you want during your purchase, especially when buying a home abroad. The procedure in Spain is also quite different: whereas in the Netherlands the seller pays the selling agent and the buyer pays the buying agent, in Spain the sale price includes a percentage that is shared between the selling and buying agent (except in the Valencia region).</p><p>As a buyer, it is important to know what you actually pay your buyer’s agent and what they do for it. Property Consultancy Spain is transparent about this. Based on your wishes we make a selection of suitable homes and point out the amenities in different neighbourhoods or in the region where you are looking. Our consultants will inform you about the costs in advance.</p><p>Unfortunately Spain is something of a jungle of estate agents, including some without experience. Our team, however, has been working in European real estate for more than 20 years, and our consultants often hold legal or real-estate qualifications. At PC-Spain you can count on the support of an expert who represents your interests throughout the purchase. And because we speak Dutch, English and Spanish, we can bridge the language and cultural differences.</p><p>You can also hire a buyer’s agent once you have already found your ideal home in Spain. The agent then advises you on the price and helps you with the next steps. By attending the viewing, we uncover the strengths and weaknesses of the house for you, and use them to help you negotiate the price. Our consultants also help you get the paperwork in order.</p><h2>The advantages of a Dutch agent in Spain</h2><p>Hiring a buyer’s agent is a good choice, especially in a housing market that is unfamiliar to you, like Spain’s. So what exactly are the advantages of a Dutch property consultant in Spain?</p><p>First, the <a href="{A_('de-beste-nederlandse-makelaar-in-spanje')}">Dutch buyer’s agent</a> knows the Spanish housing market well – probably a lot better than you do. That makes it easy for the consultant to estimate the value of a home, and their experience in negotiating means you will end up paying a fair and good price.</p><p>Another advantage is that an agent is not emotionally involved in the purchase. Of course they know your wishes, but they can keep looking at the home rationally and point out any drawbacks, to prevent problems in the future.</p><p>A final advantage is that a Dutch buyer’s agent in Spain also looks at the legal side. Spain has its own laws and regulations around buying a house, and a property consultant will inform you about them. They also arrange the paperwork and make sure your documents are ready for the purchase.</p><p>Are you ready to take the step? Get in touch. We would be happy to help you buy your Spanish home!</p>'''),
 'de-beste-nederlandse-makelaar-in-spanje': ('Dutch estate agent in Spain', f'''<p>Looking for the best Dutch property consultant in Spain? Makes sense. Buying a house is a big investment and you want expert advice – especially in a foreign country, with a foreign language and a different way of doing things (think of the siesta and an appointment culture of ‘mañana, mañana’). As a Dutch agent in Spain we know both cultures well, as well as the laws and regulations for buying a home. With us as your partner you can go through the process in your own language; your property consultant translates everything into Spanish language and customs.</p><p>With our knowledge and experience we advise you on the purchase and support you in making an offer. We guide you through the entire buying process, are always available for questions and go that extra mile for you. Want to learn more about the best property consultant in Spain? Read on or <a href="en-intake.html">get in touch</a>.</p><h2>Buying a house in Spain</h2><p>Buying a house is an important step in your life. That is true in the Netherlands, and even more so when you want to buy abroad. It brings risks and uncertainty, mainly because you are often not familiar with the laws of that country. An agent can help: they take you by the hand and guide you through the whole process. So want to buy a home abroad? Hire a property consultant. It saves you time, effort and a bad purchase.</p><p>Have you set your heart on a house in Spain – the warm, welcoming country where the kitchen always smells good? You will find a wide choice of houses and apartments. Whether you are looking for an authentic Spanish villa or an apartment in the centre of, say, Valencia, as a Dutch agent in Spain we are your partner in buying your home.</p><h2>Your Spanish home through a Dutch consultant in Spain</h2><p>Spain is a huge country, more than 12 times the size of the Netherlands. The culture is different, and so is the housing market – and there are big differences between its 17 regions, including in the homes themselves. So what should you look for in your search for your ideal Spanish home? A property consultant helps you set out realistic wishes that fit your budget. By asking the right questions, Property Consultancy Spain finds out what you are looking for in a home.</p><p>We search for property in the region you prefer, matching your wishes and budget. As the best agent in Spain we make the search for your ideal home a great success. Whether your Spanish home should be on the beach, right in the centre or in a picturesque village, we will find it for you.</p>'''),
 'hoeveel-eigen-geld-om-een-woning-te-kopen-in-spanje': ('How much of your own money do you need?', '''<p>Do you want to buy a home in Spain, to live in or as an investment, but don’t know how much of your own money you need to put in? Don’t worry – we are happy to tell you. Applying for a mortgage in Spain works differently from the Netherlands. Our team is ready to answer all your legal and financing questions, and when you are ready to buy, you can contact us too. Our consultants specialise in several fields related to buying homes in Spain.</p><h2>How much of my own money do I need?</h2><p>You may have savings, liquid assets or equity in your home in the Netherlands, but there is a good chance you will need a mortgage to finance a home in Spain. For that you apply to a Spanish bank. A non-resident – so you, as a Dutch citizen – can receive a private mortgage of up to 70%. Through a company (BV) you can get a 50% mortgage. The Spanish bank calculates the mortgage on the lower of the purchase price and the valuation. So if the valuation comes in below the purchase price, the bank bases the mortgage on the valuation, which can change the amount of your own money you need.</p><p>For your own funds, this means you must finance at least 30% of the amount yourself. That is different if you emigrate to Spain and are already registered as a resident: then you can borrow up to 80%, so you finance 20% yourself. Buyer’s costs are never included in the financing.</p><p>An example: you want to buy a home of 200,000 euros in Valencia. What you need is…</p><h2>Buying a home in Spain with your own money</h2><p>So you need a reasonable amount of your own capital to buy a home in Spain. That doesn’t make the step any less worthwhile. Spain is a beautiful country where the sun shines 320 days a year. Whether you are looking for a second home or emigrating, buying property in Spain is a dream for many. To make that dream come true, our team of buyer’s agents is ready for you. We help you get to know the Spanish housing market, with the legal questions, the negotiation and the final steps to make the home yours.</p><p>Do you have questions about buying property in Spain, are you curious about the additional costs, or are you ready to start the buying process? Get in touch – we would be happy to talk to you!</p>'''),
 'huis-kopen-in-spanje-bijkomende-kosten': ('Property in Spain – additional costs', '''<p>Buying property in Spain comes with additional costs, just like in the Netherlands. Curious what they are exactly? We are happy to tell you. Buying a home is not something you do lightly, especially a second home abroad, so it is important to know which expenses to expect. Here is an overview of the taxes and other costs.</p><h2>Costs for a new-build home in Spain</h2><p>It is important to know that Spain has two rates for tax and therefore for buyer’s costs. When you buy a new-build home in Spain, the buyer’s costs are about 14.5% of the purchase price. Most of that is VAT and the tax you pay for recording the notarial deeds, which is 10%.</p><h2>Costs for buying an existing home</h2><p>When you buy an existing home in Spain, you don’t pay VAT but Spanish transfer tax (ITP). The rate varies by region, but is between 12% and 14% of the purchase price.</p><h2>Registration tax on your second home</h2><p>Besides VAT or transfer tax, you also pay registration tax on the purchase of a second home in Spain. It pays the notary for registering your house in the Spanish land registry. The amount varies by region, but expect a few hundred euros.</p><h2>Buying a Spanish home with good guidance</h2><p>So there are several taxes to take into account, plus mortgage and valuation costs, which vary a lot depending on your wishes. For more information we are happy to refer you to our consultants, who are ready to answer all your questions and get started on your Spanish home. With our personal approach we guide you through the entire buying process, offering both purchase and legal guidance, which makes the process easier for you. Let’s start the search for your ideal home!</p>'''),
 'huis-kopen-in-spanje': ('Buying a home in Spain', '''<h2>Buying property in Spain</h2><p>Are you ready to take the step – to leave the Netherlands behind, wholly or partly, and move to Spain? Whether you are emigrating or buying a second home to escape the harsh winters, buying a house in Spain is a special and exciting step. That is why we want your search to go smoothly. Our team of experienced buyer’s agents helps you, with expert purchase guidance as well as legal advice and support. That ensures a transparent buying process, so you can buy your ideal home, loft or studio in Spain.</p><h2>An agent for your purchase in Spain</h2><p>Buying a house involves all kinds of things – as you probably remember from your last purchase in the Netherlands. Abroad, however, things work differently, with other laws and rules. That is why it is wise to hire an agent.</p><p>An agent helps you on several fronts. They can support you at the start of your search for a home in Spain, drawing up a list of all your wishes for the house, including your preferred location, nearby amenities and the size of the plot. The agent then makes a selection of available homes and sends it to you.</p><p>You can also choose to hire an agent later, for example once you have found a home yourself. The agent then helps you with the next steps, which mainly means doing everything possible to get you that home: advising you on the price and helping you negotiate. An agent also helps you get all the paperwork in order – they know what you need to buy a house in Spain!</p><h2>Buying your ideal home in Spain</h2><p>Whether you want to buy a house in Valencia or on the Costa Blanca, buying your ideal home in Spain doesn’t have to be complicated. Our experienced team of buyer’s agents is happy to help. We know the Spanish housing market well and are up to date on all the laws around buying a house in Spain, so we can advise you well and take the right steps, so the buying process doesn’t stall or fall through. Our knowledge also lets us judge the value of a home, which gives us an advantage when negotiating the price.</p><p>So there are several advantages to hiring a buyer’s agent. As a Dutch buyer’s agent, Property Consultancy Spain is a good partner during your purchase. Curious how exactly we can help? Get in touch and we will bring you closer to your ideal Spanish home!</p>'''),
 'huis-kopen-spanje-wat-moet-je-weten': ('Buying a home in Spain: what should you know?', '''<p>Buying a house is not something you do lightly, especially abroad. Buying property in Spain is an exciting step that deserves good preparation. What should you know about buying a home in Spain? To help you on your way, we are happy to share what the buying process looks like. We have years of experience as a Dutch buyer’s agent in Spain, because we believe everyone deserves a smooth purchase with as few problems and uncertainties as possible.</p><h2>Finding your home in Spain</h2><p>The procedure for buying a home in Spain starts with the search, and it is important to know exactly what you want – you can’t just pop round to view a house. How many rooms do you want, which location do you prefer and which amenities do you want nearby? Still unsure? A buyer’s agent can help you get clear on what you are looking for. Together with you they draw up a wish list and select homes based on it, saving you a lot of time and effort. An agent knows the Spanish housing market like no other and finds the hidden gems for you.</p><p>Have your eye on a home? Then it is time to view it. An agent books the viewing trip for you and offers help and advice along the way, so you can be sure of making the right choice.</p><h2>How do you buy a house in Spain?</h2><p>Was the viewing a success and are you excited about the house? Then it is time to negotiate – and here too a buyer’s agent is a partner you want on your side. An agent has a lot of experience in negotiating the purchase price and can often get you a good deal. But they help with more than negotiating: they also inform you about all the costs of buying a Spanish home. You need your own funds, of course, but you also pay taxes and recurring costs. The agent arranges the documents you need and provides legal guidance, which makes buying a house in Spain a lot easier.</p><h2>Buying a Spanish home through an agent</h2><p>We have listed several reasons why it is wise to hire an agent when buying your house in Spain: the process becomes much simpler for you. We take care of everything during the purchase, because our team specialises in several fields, offering both purchase guidance and legal guidance. That keeps the process transparent. We make clear agreements and make sure you find your dream home in Spain. Want more information or ready to take the step? Get in touch!</p>'''),
 'hulp-bij-woning-aankoop-spanje': ('Help with buying a home in Spain', '''<p>Buying a home in Spain is an exciting step, and for Dutch-speaking buyers the process isn’t always clear. The laws and regulations are different, another language is spoken and Spanish culture differs from Dutch culture. So it is very helpful to get expert help in that foreign country in your own language, from reliable, qualified and experienced consultants who know the procedures and can answer all your questions, for example about the mortgage. Would you like help finding and buying a home or investment in Spain? We will help you through the buying process, with both purchase guidance and legal advice, which makes it much easier for you.</p><h2>The procedure for buying a home in Spain</h2><p>To prepare you for what lies ahead, here is the procedure. Would you like our help with buying your home in Spain? We start with an introductory meeting. We want all your questions answered and to learn about your wishes. Because every home has different features and every client different wishes, our advice is tailored. Then we search for the ideal home for you in Spain. Once we have found it, we schedule a viewing – and of course we provide help and advice on your viewing trip and go with you.</p><p>Meanwhile our legal department is already at work. They check all the details, such as registrations and (occupancy) permits, and look into the background of the landlord/seller. You will also need to supply documents for this; we will let you know in good time so you can send them.</p><p>Once everything is in order and you are still excited about the home, we make an offer. We handle the negotiations on the purchase price – in consultation with you, of course, with clear agreements. Has your offer been accepted? Then we also finalise matters such as the financing with the Spanish bank. Finally, it is time for a toast – because we celebrate success together!</p><h2>Applying for a mortgage for a home in Spain</h2><p>If you need a mortgage to buy your home in Spain, we help with that too, through our Dutch partner Spaanse Hypotheek. They have several banks in their network and offer independent mortgage advice, so you know whether you need a mortgage or not. If so, they help you apply. We make not only the purchase but also the mortgage application simpler – which makes us your partner for buying property in Spain!</p>'''),
 'kosten-bij-aankoop-huis-in-spanje': ('Costs of buying a house in Spain', '''<p>When you want to buy a house in Spain, it is important to have an idea of the budget you want to spend. In Spain, as in the Netherlands, there are “buyer’s costs”, and there are other costs as well. Curious which costs come with buying a house in Spain? We are happy to explain them, and you can also contact us for more information.</p><h2>Buyer’s costs when buying a house in Spain</h2><p>Buyer’s costs are around 12 to 14 percent of the purchase price. For new builds in Spain they are up to about 14.5 percent. That includes everything: notary fees, registration fees, taxes, stamp duty and the lawyer’s fee.</p><p><strong>We are happy to explain each of these costs separately.</strong></p><ul><li>In Spain too, the notary is an official office, so the fees are regulated. The amount depends on the purchase price, but usually lies between €600 and €900.</li></ul><ul><li>Property registration is also regulated and usually costs between €400 and €650.</li></ul><ul><li>Transfer tax is 10 percent of the purchase price. For new builds this is VAT (IVA in Spain); for existing homes it is transfer tax, or ITP. Lower rates can apply in exceptional cases, but these are very rare, especially for a second home.</li></ul><ul><li>Stamp duty is levied on new properties and calculated on the notary and registration costs. Each autonomous community has its own rates, between 0.5 and 1.5 percent of the purchase price.</li></ul><h2>The costs of buying your dream home in Spain</h2><p>Do you have a clear picture of the costs and are you ready to start the search for your house in Spain? We are your reliable buyer’s agent for this adventure. With our personal approach and expertise in several fields we can guide you through the entire buying process, with purchase guidance as well as legal guidance, which makes it easier for you. Want more information about the costs of buying a house in Spain, or about the procedure? Get in touch. Our experienced team of buyer’s agents is happy to help, and with your wishes in mind we will bring you closer to your dream home in Spain!</p>'''),
 'nederlandse-makelaar-in-valencia': ('Dutch estate agent in Valencia', '''<p>A house in a country where the sun shines 320 days a year and it is almost always warm – who wouldn’t want that? As a Dutch agent in Spain we help you find a home in the beautiful city of Valencia, where you can choose a location in the city centre, on the beach or along the lovely Turia, for example. Whether you are looking for a second home for the winter or emigrating to Valencia, you don’t want to run into too many obstacles during the search and purchase. We make sure the process runs smoothly. Our consultants know the city inside out and are happy to help you buy property in Valencia. They know the do’s and don’ts and know the different neighbourhoods like the back of their hand. Benefit from our service – we are always there for you, so that you can soon enjoy your Spanish home!</p><h2>Buying a home in Valencia</h2><p>Valencia is the third-largest city in Spain: a beautiful, vibrant city on the Balearic Sea (part of the Mediterranean). Valencia has everything you need in daily life, so it is no surprise you want to buy a home here! It has a lively old town with many museums and churches. The beautiful centre full of shops can keep you busy all day, and there is also a large city park and of course a promenade for lovely walks.</p><p>Whether you are moving to escape the cold winters or perhaps to start a business in Spain, Valencia is a great choice. You will want for nothing here.</p><h2>Buying through a Dutch agent in Valencia</h2><p>What you need to bear in mind when buying a home in Valencia is the process you have to go through. Buying property involves many different steps. That is often a hassle in the Netherlands, let alone in a country where you may not speak the language and where other laws and rules apply. Buying a home in Valencia takes time and effort, but it certainly doesn’t have to be the end of your Spanish adventure – we are happy to simplify the buying process for you.</p><p>We inform you about the relevant laws and regulations for buying a home in Spain and guide you personally through the entire buying process. We stay in active contact and think along with you, taking all your wishes and requirements into account during the house search. That is how we find the right home in Valencia for you.</p><h2>Find your ideal home in Valencia</h2><p>Valencia offers a wide choice of houses and apartments. We get to work based on your wishes and find a suitable home for you. Location plays an important role: do you want to be close to the beach or right in the centre of Valencia? Whatever your preference, we help you make the right choice. Our consultants go that extra mile: we come along to viewings and help with the negotiation and with making an offer. Good news? Then of course we celebrate together. Get in touch now and we will start the search for your ideal home in Spain straight away!</p>'''),
 'onbezorgd-een-woning-kopen-in-spanje': ('Buying a home in Spain without worries', '''<p>We guide you in buying your ideal home in Spain. We do this because we are passionate about our work and in love with the country where you are looking for a home. As Dutch agents in Spain we are your partner in buying a home in Spain, and we are committed to making it a worry-free period for you – whether you are looking for a place to spend the winter or you are emigrating. We guide you through orientation and the search for your dream home, taking into account your wishes such as location, size, layout and year of construction. That is how we find the home that suits you perfectly!</p><h2>Purchase guidance in Spain</h2><p>As agents we take the work off your hands, so you can concentrate fully on viewing homes. First we make a selection of homes based on your wishes. Interested in one or more? We make the appointments with the agents and go to the viewings with you. We support you and look at the bigger picture: what condition is the home in? How does the asking price compare to the home itself? Everything you might not think of at first, we do for you, so all your questions are answered and you get a complete picture of the homes.</p><p>Then, if you are excited about a home, we support you in making an offer. Through our network and knowledge we know the housing market, so we help you decide on the right amount. The housing market in Spain, like in the Netherlands, is extremely competitive. By working with us you choose convenience as well as the assurance of a good choice. We guide you from A to Z – we tell you honestly when a house isn’t worth the money, but we go all out for you once you have found your dream home. In short, we are there for you throughout your search for a home in Spain.</p><h2>Letting your holiday home in Spain</h2><p>Do you want to buy a Spanish home as a second home, a nice place to spend the winter? Then it may be worth looking at the options for letting it as a holiday home. Many people do this and let their home in high season, which makes it a good investment. Curious about the possibilities? Get in touch – we can inform and advise you about this step.</p><p>Want to buy a home in Spain without worries? Then we are your partner. We point out the pitfalls, objectively assess the condition and value of the home and stand by you throughout the buying process. Get in touch when you are ready for your next step towards Spain!</p>'''),
 'procedure-aankoop-woning-spanje': ('Procedure for buying a home in Spain', '''<p>We guide you in buying your ideal home in Spain. We do this because we are passionate about our work and in love with the country where you are looking for a home. We are committed to making your property purchase a worry-free period – whether you are looking for a (second) home for yourself or want to make a smart investment.</p><h2>The search for a home</h2><p>When you join Property Consultancy Spain, we schedule a call or an appointment in person in the Netherlands or Spain. In this conversation we explain how things work and discuss your wishes regarding location, size, layout and year of construction. We share our own experience, but above all we listen to which features matter to you. Together we see whether we can lay a good foundation for working together. We then send you the start-up invoice.</p><p>Once we have agreed what you want to buy, we make several homes available through our partners (after that invoice has been paid). We plan two to three days in Spain to drive around with you in person and view homes. During these viewings you can expect plenty of advice from us, to help you make the best choice.</p><p>If you are looking for property as an investment, we only show you properties that are suitable for it. If you are looking for a second home, we also explore the area together to see whether the region suits you.</p><h2>The purchase procedure for your Spanish home</h2><p>Once you have found your ideal Spanish home during the viewings, we make sure it becomes yours. Before an offer is made, you are first informed about all purchase costs, other recurring costs and taxes, so you can decide properly whether you can and want to make an offer. Of course, as your buyer’s agent we are there for you in this decision. Together we decide on a strategy so we make the right offer. Our team then starts the negotiations, aiming for the best price and/or terms.</p><p>During this process we also help you apply for an NIE number, the Spanish tax number you need before the purchase takes place. We help you open a Spanish bank account and put you in touch with a lawyer – and, in the case of an investment, a tax adviser or gestor. Our consultants help you draw up a reservation contract and review all the property documents to get a clear picture of the condition of the home and the permits. When everything is in order, we book a date with the notary.</p><p>Unfortunately no suitable home among them? Then we will do our best over the following months to find one after all, either with you on location or by video call if you are not in Spain yourself.</p><h2>A provisional purchase contract</h2><p>Depending on the seller’s terms, there may first be a provisional purchase contract (Contrato de Arras Penitenciales). You usually pay a 10% deposit of the purchase price after 45 days. This is paid to the seller, a contract is drawn up, and the date of the transfer is agreed.</p><p>We hope the procedure for buying a home in Spain is now a bit clearer. If not, you can always contact us. We are happy to explain everything down to the last detail, so you are assured of a pleasant and clear buying process.</p>'''),
 'uitleg-aankoop-commissie-spanje': ('Purchase commission in Spain explained', '''<p>Scouring the Spanish housing market for your ideal home is an exciting time – one that asks a lot of you, in both energy and effort. You are often unfamiliar with Spanish laws and regulations, and the whole buying process can be overwhelming. That is why many people choose to hire a buyer’s agent, who helps you in both the orientation phase and the purchase, making the process a lot easier. But an agent doesn’t work for nothing. Here we explain the purchase commission in Spain – the amount an agent charges for their services.</p><h2>Why does a buyer’s agent charge commission?</h2><p>First it helps to understand what a buyer’s agent actually does. Buying a home in Spain involves a lot. An agent is your partner throughout the process and takes care of everything. They scour the Spanish housing market for you and find gems that match your wishes. Once they have found your ideal house, they move on to the negotiation and achieve a cost saving for you. For their time and effort, they charge a commission.</p><h2>Agents’ commission in Spain</h2><p>In Spain the commission for the buying and selling agents is usually included in the purchase price, so the visible price includes commission. As a Dutch buyer’s agent in Spain, we share this commission with you. We believe our cooperation should be transparent, so we are not secretive about our rates. We share the difference between the purchase price before and after our mediation: when we save on the initial asking price – our profit – we share it with the client. That gives you a discount on the purchase price.</p><h2>Buying a home in Spain through Property Consultancy Spain</h2><p>Transparent amounts and sharp negotiations. We are committed to getting a fair, market-based price for buyer and seller, using our knowledge and experience to achieve it. By negotiating we realise a saving on the purchase price for you – and, just as with the commission, we share that saving. Want more information about our purchase commission, or about commissions in Spain in general? Get in touch. Our team of experienced buyer’s agents is happy to help!</p>'''),
}
